  "mechanism": "do_sys_readv/do_sys_writev call the scalar file.read/file.write once per iovec, and InodeHandle takes and releases the shared offset lock per scalar call, so a competitor on a dup'd descriptor can commit between two iovecs of one vector call.",
  "sites": [
    "kernel/core/src/syscall/preadv.rs::do_sys_readv",
    "kernel/core/src/syscall/pwritev.rs::do_sys_writev",
    "kernel/core/src/fs/file/inode_handle.rs::InodeHandle::read",
    "kernel/core/src/fs/file/inode_handle.rs::InodeHandle::write"
  ],
