  "contract": "readv(2)/writev(2): a vector transfer on one open file description is atomic with respect to other I/O through that description (Linux holds f_pos_lock for the whole call).",
  "observed": "Asterinas lets a concurrent read or write on a dup'd descriptor land between two iovecs of one readv/writev (79 to 98 of 100 rounds torn at SMP=2).",
